    {
      "text": "Try again. Check the piece name and tap the marked square.",
      "normalized": "try again check the piece name and tap the marked square",
      "file": "audio/f7ae03dd827c81f3a0a4ecc4.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "Use the Pawn to capture the opponent’s piece on e5.",
      "normalized": "use the pawn to capture the opponent s piece on e5",
      "file": "audio/bfe5a9349aa0e61400f71397.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "Use the Rook to capture the opponent’s piece on g4.",
      "normalized": "use the rook to capture the opponent s piece on g4",
      "file": "audio/5e0734785aa570d2c9508cea.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "We see the board from White’s side. The bottom-right square is light. Place the white pieces first, then the black pieces.",
      "normalized": "we see the board from white s side the bottom right square is light place the white pieces first then the black pieces",
      "file": "audio/8f81d1148d3c720799337556.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "When in check, you must remove the threat. Select the king on e1 and move it to the safe square d1.",
      "normalized": "when in check you must remove the threat select the king on e1 and move it to the safe square d1",
      "file": "audio/1bb7d70289fe7f6db9a13dfe.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "White",
      "normalized": "white",
      "file": "audio/018fa96a44715c90bf93be14.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "White bishop moved from",
      "normalized": "white bishop moved from",
      "file": "audio/eb1e8b6f004278dadcfb3d4e.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "White king moved from",
      "normalized": "white king moved from",
      "file": "audio/adcf033ff2b972d55db297e5.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "White knight moved from",
      "normalized": "white knight moved from",
      "file": "audio/6c4fc948677887e28b783307.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "White pawn moved from",
      "normalized": "white pawn moved from",
      "file": "audio/73ce6da1c81ef65657dfac84.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "White pieces",
      "normalized": "white pieces",
      "file": "audio/2c09a48994e20c4dd5787689.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "White queen moved from",
      "normalized": "white queen moved from",
      "file": "audio/4eeef3a4964f37e22023d80a.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "White rook moved from",
      "normalized": "white rook moved from",
      "file": "audio/05d004d16d7e14bb45001b76.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "White to move. Choose the white king’s situation.",
      "normalized": "white to move choose the white king s situation",
      "file": "audio/5569640994c6cfc8043d94fd.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "White to move. Select a white piece and checkmate the black king in one move.",
      "normalized": "white to move select a white piece and checkmate the black king in one move",
      "file": "audio/2cf4046683cb68876bf2c4cd.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "You can also protect the king by capturing the attacker. Select the bishop on h1 and capture the black rook on e4.",
      "normalized": "you can also protect the king by capturing the attacker select the bishop on h1 and capture the black rook on e4",
      "file": "audio/b39ce75ba20f17aa2cd7ce88.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "You can block a distant attack. Select the rook on a2 and move it to e2 to protect your king.",
      "normalized": "you can block a distant attack select the rook on a2 and move it to e2 to protect your king",
      "file": "audio/e3d880365d74f53ffc09332a.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "You completed every task! You can play them again.",
      "normalized": "you completed every task you can play them again",
      "file": "audio/9d10a7b2460a2781b9757884.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "You won!",
      "normalized": "you won",
      "file": "audio/54a2e1aeb5555de8eea78faf.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "An opening is the beginning of a game. Learn the ideas, then explore famous examples on the board.",
      "normalized": "an opening is the beginning of a game learn the ideas then explore famous examples on the board",
      "file": "audio/6bda8220ed92510ab81a1ec8.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "Use central pawns and pieces to control the middle. The four central squares are e4, d4, e5 and d5.",
      "normalized": "use central pawns and pieces to control the middle the four central squares are e4 d4 e5 and d5",
      "file": "audio/f1fadbc2ff49ec5c08532796.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bring knights and bishops into play. Usually, develop several pieces instead of moving the same one repeatedly.",
      "normalized": "bring knights and bishops into play usually develop several pieces instead of moving the same one repeatedly",
      "file": "audio/63957bbd4319e7bb9b7dc514.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "Prepare to castle when it is legal and safe. Connect your rooks and avoid exposing your king.",
      "normalized": "prepare to castle when it is legal and safe connect your rooks and avoid exposing your king",
      "file": "audio/ae019f389c08e61d21467f33.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "Before every move, look for checks, captures and threats from both sides. An opening name does not make a move safe.",
      "normalized": "before every move look for checks captures and threats from both sides an opening name does not make a move safe",
      "file": "audio/554637d64239183625e966fc.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "Italian Game",
      "normalized": "italian game",
      "file": "audio/cddcaf50932385b263a6996d.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "Develop the knight to f3 and bishop to c4. The bishop looks toward f7, while White prepares to castle. Black can answer in several ways.",
      "normalized": "develop the knight to f3 and bishop to c4 the bishop looks toward f7 while white prepares to castle black can answer in several ways",
      "file": "audio/7cbb2e21b1945097cde3f7cc.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ruy Lopez (Spanish Opening)",
      "normalized": "ruy lopez spanish opening",
      "file": "audio/bca3acb3c0cd5c4037708b45.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "The bishop goes to b5 and pressures the knight defending e5. Our example continues with a6, asking the bishop to decide where to go.",
      "normalized": "the bishop goes to b5 and pressures the knight defending e5 our example continues with a6 asking the bishop to decide where to go",
      "file": "audio/2eabec9e6504638650cc2764.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "Scotch Game",
      "normalized": "scotch game",
      "file": "audio/8d2b18b790d7f6aebd26c6e9.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "White challenges the center early with d4. After the pawn exchange, the knight recaptures on d4 and takes an active central square.",
      "normalized": "white challenges the center early with d4 after the pawn exchange the knight recaptures on d4 and takes an active central square",
      "file": "audio/76b9551c2d3fa16cb47533ee.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "Queen's Gambit",
      "normalized": "queen s gambit",
      "file": "audio/e10d18e3b1568245e3e4bd91.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "White offers the c-pawn to challenge Black's d5-pawn. Black can accept or decline; this example declines with e6 and develops pieces.",
      "normalized": "white offers the c pawn to challenge black s d5 pawn black can accept or decline this example declines with e6 and develops pieces",
      "file": "audio/a51301e619215420be02df4f.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "London System",
      "normalized": "london system",
      "file": "audio/049e8e346c7d9dd030cf6279.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "White develops the dark-squared bishop to f4 before playing e3. Build a steady center, but adapt the plan to Black's moves.",
      "normalized": "white develops the dark squared bishop to f4 before playing e3 build a steady center but adapt the plan to black s moves",
      "file": "audio/0031ed0ac011e570cfbd7faf.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sicilian Defense",
      "normalized": "sicilian defense",
      "file": "audio/efbeb0b1b68a2fb610398e59.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "Black answers e4 with c5 to contest d4 from the side. This Open Sicilian example exchanges pawns and brings White's knight to d4.",
      "normalized": "black answers e4 with c5 to contest d4 from the side this open sicilian example exchanges pawns and brings white s knight to d4",
      "file": "audio/657722372f41a9c4fa75b7bd.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "French Defense",
      "normalized": "french defense",
      "file": "audio/0210fc6f13d52f73cb1d07fe.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "Black prepares d5 with e6. In this Advance Variation, White gains space with e5 and Black challenges the center with c5.",
      "normalized": "black prepares d5 with e6 in this advance variation white gains space with e5 and black challenges the center with c5",
      "file": "audio/0caf505b9551f610e8f53f60.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "Caro-Kann Defense",
      "normalized": "caro kann defense",
      "file": "audio/26efd4e89e5a41a2af1d2ffd.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "Black prepares d5 with c6. In this example, Black captures on e4 and White recaptures with a knight; both sides still need to develop.",
      "normalized": "black prepares d5 with c6 in this example black captures on e4 and white recaptures with a knight both sides still need to develop",
      "file": "audio/6972ccb71204fcc4c3969bbd.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "This pawn move fights for control of the center and gives the pieces more room.",
      "normalized": "this pawn move fights for control of the center and gives the pieces more room",
      "file": "audio/e8e70c04b56d1e899b30659c.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "A minor piece joins the game and influences important squares.",
      "normalized": "a minor piece joins the game and influences important squares",
      "file": "audio/80d8a1765d162cf9515ae65c.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "This move challenges an opposing piece or the opponent's control of the center.",
      "normalized": "this move challenges an opposing piece or the opponent s control of the center",
      "file": "audio/589455430772d4a585b4bf43.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "This pawn move supports the central structure or prepares another central pawn move.",
      "normalized": "this pawn move supports the central structure or prepares another central pawn move",
      "file": "audio/4da830fc36944ca6b12cb464.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "A capture changes the center. Notice which piece or pawn takes its place.",
      "normalized": "a capture changes the center notice which piece or pawn takes its place",
      "file": "audio/96e3b876d991244eb924a40f.mp3"
    },
    {
      "text": "The pawn advances to gain space. Check how the opponent can challenge the pawn chain.",
      "normalized": "the pawn advances to gain space check how the opponent can challenge the pawn chain",
      "file": "audio/f70aa6fbe88c39778dc4d57a.mp3"
    }
  ]
